451
00:16:43,215 --> 00:16:45,702
Three auctions is a tiny sample,

452
00:16:45,702 --> 00:16:47,879
and the Time Attack car is a

453
00:16:47,879 --> 00:16:50,833
special version, so we cannot say what

454
00:16:50,833 --> 00:16:52,932
an average Nevera is worth.

455
00:16:53,112 --> 00:16:54,581
But it fits a pattern:

456
00:16:54,581 --> 00:16:56,584
bids well below the new price.

457
00:16:56,934 --> 00:16:59,075
There is an important lesson in how

458
00:16:59,075 --> 00:16:59,871
to read this.

459
00:17:00,051 --> 00:17:03,195
Hypercars often hold their value because they

460
00:17:03,195 --> 00:17:03,824
are rare.

461
00:17:04,004 --> 00:17:07,386
Wikipedia says only one hundred fifty Neveras

462
00:17:07,386 --> 00:17:08,288
are planned.

463
00:17:08,468 --> 00:17:10,936
Yet these results show that rarity alone

464
00:17:10,936 --> 00:17:12,601
does not guarantee a price.

465
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:14,214
A new technology,

466
00:17:14,214 --> 00:17:15,563
and a new brand,

467
00:17:15,563 --> 00:17:17,332
carry their own risk.

468
00:17:17,683 --> 00:17:19,828
Think about the buyer on the other

469
00:17:19,828 --> 00:17:20,144
side.

470
00:17:20,324 --> 00:17:23,025
Someone who bids one million dollars on

471
00:17:23,025 --> 00:17:25,103
a used Nevera is getting a car

472
00:17:25,103 --> 00:17:27,735
with fewer than fifteen hundred miles,

473
00:17:27,735 --> 00:17:28,843
a clean history,

474
00:17:28,843 --> 00:17:31,960
and the same one hundred twenty kilowatt-hour

475
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:32,514
battery.

476
00:17:32,694 --> 00:17:33,773
For that buyer,

477
00:17:33,773 --> 00:17:36,363
the drop in price is an opportunity.

478
00:17:36,543 --> 00:17:37,756
For the seller,

479
00:17:37,756 --> 00:17:38,807
it is a loss.

480
00:17:39,157 --> 00:17:41,475
There is a broader lesson here for

481
00:17:41,475 --> 00:17:43,452
electric cars of every price.

482
00:17:43,632 --> 00:17:45,549
Technology moves quickly,

483
00:17:45,549 --> 00:17:48,616
and a newer version often arrives before

484
00:17:48,616 --> 00:17:50,610
the older one is paid for.

485
00:17:50,790 --> 00:17:52,924
The Nevera R came out in August

486
00:17:52,924 --> 00:17:56,503
twenty twenty-four, only about fourteen months after

487
00:17:56,503 --> 00:17:59,257
the first deliveries to American owners,

488
00:17:59,257 --> 00:18:00,496
by our arithmetic.

489
00:18:00,846 --> 00:18:02,534
Let us put it all together,

490
00:18:02,534 --> 00:18:03,597
in our own words.

491
00:18:03,777 --> 00:18:05,954
The sticker for this car was two

492
00:18:05,954 --> 00:18:09,153
million, three hundred eleven thousand dollars.

493
00:18:09,333 --> 00:18:12,315
The electricity for its first thirteen hundred

494
00:18:12,315 --> 00:18:14,325
miles was about ninety dollars.

495
00:18:14,505 --> 00:18:16,560
The unsold bid left a gap of

496
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:18,394
over one million dollars.

497
00:18:18,574 --> 00:18:22,162
The tyres, insurance and service are unknown.

498
00:18:22,512 --> 00:18:24,837
That means the cost of an electric

499
00:18:24,837 --> 00:18:27,300
hypercar is nothing like the cost of

500
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:28,189
a normal car.

501
00:18:28,369 --> 00:18:29,644
For a family car,

502
00:18:29,644 --> 00:18:31,445
fuel and repairs matter.

503
00:18:31,625 --> 00:18:32,418
For a Nevera,

504
00:18:32,418 --> 00:18:34,856
according to every figure we could find,

505
00:18:34,856 --> 00:18:37,477
the dominant cost is the difference between

506
00:18:37,477 --> 00:18:39,549
what you pay and what someone will

507
00:18:39,549 --> 00:18:40,403
pay you later.

508
00:18:40,753 --> 00:18:43,783
And yet owners are not necessarily unhappy.

509
00:18:43,963 --> 00:18:46,339
Motor1 notes that the car came with

510
00:18:46,339 --> 00:18:47,968
a private driving coach.

511
00:18:48,148 --> 00:18:50,446
People who buy a Nevera are buying

512
00:18:50,446 --> 00:18:53,149
an experience, a place among one hundred

513
00:18:53,149 --> 00:18:56,055
fifty owners, and a record-setting machine.

514
00:18:56,235 --> 00:18:58,557
Not everything fits in a spreadsheet.

515
00:18:58,907 --> 00:19:00,288
The records are real.

516
00:19:00,468 --> 00:19:03,968
Wikipedia says the Nevera set twenty-three records

517
00:19:03,968 --> 00:19:07,187
on the seventeenth of May twenty twenty-three,

518
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:10,267
including zero to one hundred kilometres per

519
00:19:10,267 --> 00:19:12,786
hour in one point eight two seconds.

520
00:19:12,966 --> 00:19:14,847
Some buyers value that.

521
00:19:15,027 --> 00:19:17,104
Others, as the auction suggests,

522
00:19:17,104 --> 00:19:19,765
may feel differently about the price once

523
00:19:19,765 --> 00:19:21,517
the car has been delivered.

524
00:19:21,867 --> 00:19:23,527
So here is our verdict.

525
00:19:23,707 --> 00:19:25,890
If you are buying an electric hypercar,

526
00:19:25,890 --> 00:19:28,130
do not worry about the electricity bill.

527
00:19:28,310 --> 00:19:30,554
Worry about what the car will be

528
00:19:30,554 --> 00:19:31,886
worth in two years.

529
00:19:32,066 --> 00:19:34,100
If you cannot accept a loss of

530
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:35,931
a large share of the price,

531
00:19:35,931 --> 00:19:37,491
in a market this young,

532
00:19:37,491 --> 00:19:39,457
it is a decision to make with

533
00:19:39,457 --> 00:19:40,135
open eyes.

534
00:19:40,485 --> 00:19:42,133
One last caveat.

535
00:19:42,313 --> 00:19:44,709
All of this comes from one car,

536
00:19:44,709 --> 00:19:47,491
one auction, and a few price guides.

537
00:19:47,671 --> 00:19:49,239
The market could change.

538
00:19:49,419 --> 00:19:50,804
Rimac's newer cars,

539
00:19:50,804 --> 00:19:53,649
the warranty, and a growing used market

540
00:19:53,649 --> 00:19:55,618
could all move the numbers.

541
00:19:55,798 --> 00:19:58,044
We will revisit the figures when more

542
00:19:58,044 --> 00:19:59,258
sales are published.

543
00:19:59,608 --> 00:20:01,460
Do you think a Nevera will hold

544
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,835
its value in ten years?

